{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Who has ascended heaven and descended</b> — that is, who has power to ascend to the high heavens and to descend to the earth that is below; I do not know by my wisdom." "<b>In his hollow hands</b> — so that the hearer will understand that his hollow hands and his hands are his will or his intellect, that is, that he gathers the wind so that it does not blow." "<b>Who has gathered the waters</b> — as if he gathered them in clouds that resemble a garment, to rain upon the earth." "<b>All the ends of the earth</b> — that they not be shaken; and the ends are the extremities that stand on nothing." "<b>What is his name</b> — for their sons have not attained to his name and to his knowledge; even I, for I am of them. And now two things I have asked of you." "<b>What is his name and what is his son's name</b> — that he knows Him in his wisdom." "<b>If you know</b> — you, Ithiel the man or his son: tell me one name of them that he knows. And the meaning: he cannot know Him, and there is none among the created beings that knows Him in His wisdom."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:30.937160041Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}